From: WineDroid
Subject: [PATCH] wine.inf: Make the Android driver the default graphics driver.

The desktop that WineActivity starts gets the android driver on
explorer's command line, but explorer picks the driver of any other
desktop from HKCU\Software\Wine\Drivers\Graphics, which was unset, so it
fell back to "mac,x11,wayland". Chromium's sandbox (Chrome, VS Code and
other Electron apps) starts its renderers on a desktop of their own, and
the explorer for that desktop got no working driver: the renderers never
got going and VS Code webviews such as the Claude Code panel stayed
blank. Default to android; 0x2 keeps a value the user set.
---
diff --git a/loader/wine.inf.in b/loader/wine.inf.in
--- a/loader/wine.inf.in
+++ b/loader/wine.inf.in
@@ -558,6 +558,7 @@ HKLM,%MciExtStr%,"wvx",,"MPEGVideo"
 
 [Misc]
 HKCU,Software\Wine\DllOverrides,"conpty",0x2,"builtin"
+HKCU,Software\Wine\Drivers,"Graphics",0x2,"android"
 HKLM,Software\Borland\Database Engine\Settings\SYSTEM\INIT,SHAREDMEMLOCATION,,9000
 HKLM,Software\Clients,,16
 HKLM,Software\Clients\Mail,,2,"Native Mail Client"
